        details = "Keeps: advert-free licence funding of Nordic social democracy (BBC licence fee and advert-free broadcasting, a newspaper history); open ownership judged by variety in Classical laissez-faire capitalism and Monetarist neoliberalism (Newspaper ownership concentration and content variety, a single preprint). Blocks: a state objection that froze a rise in the fee (Germany's household licence fee and the dispute over its rise), safeguarded by a rule that the fee rises unless parliament overrides it by a set majority within a fixed time; state steering of news (Mercantilism), safeguarded by a multi-party board with fixed terms and no ministry role in programming. Test: over five years, measure independent ownership of local news outlets, audience reach of public and private news, years between fee decisions and complaints of political interference. Source: Irish News, 'A history of the TV licence fee' (2020); Lisa George, preprint on arXiv (2001); European Audiovisual Observatory, IRIS Merlin legal updates (2025 and 2026); The Local, news reports (2010 and 2024); Heckscher, Mercantilism.",
    ),
)
